[{:db/id "q-316355/field-1/29cc2f60e638121dd3fb8bc1724b0279bf17e7592b74b565aa2956d4b2014422" :answer/id #uuid "38ea67c4-0751-5480-ae88-46e81a19c605" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{31}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316355/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "efb6b3d3-1ae5-5706-bfd4-2b865e7bfded" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316355/field-1/29cc2f60e638121dd3fb8bc1724b0279bf17e7592b74b565aa2956d4b2014422" :answer-field/choices ["q-316355/field-1/29cc2f60e638121dd3fb8bc1724b0279bf17e7592b74b565aa2956d4b2014422"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316355" :question/id #uuid "ec8f22dc-8840-55ee-9227-a4bca5d5e953" :question/math-academy-id "q-316355" :question/problem "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the triangle spanned by $p=⟨0,5,-1⟩$ and $q=⟨6,0,1⟩.$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\times q & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 5 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(5\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)i-(0\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 6)j+(0\\cdot 0-5\\cdot 6)k \\\\  & =5i-6j-30k \\\\  & =⟨5,-6,-30⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,p\\times q\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(-30)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+36+900} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{961} \\\\  & =31.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{31}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-316355/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88dd688-449b-5a6d-8b91-78d00d0c932b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316355"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316345/field-1/1c985c8ab9f6595267f155c1c2d55523186e5b9f7a2b779f2a5f7673f6c4ac53" :answer/id #uuid "11902f40-460a-54f5-ba02-3fcc03bf928d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316345/field-1/1ecb89157a2da3b6e808df0f3926c29bf711ed3aea432ed0b84fde5c0990b06c" :answer/id #uuid "c1fa1e7c-e0e2-5a3a-9a9c-162f9105c39b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "425" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316345/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "943d052b-f729-5c2a-b57b-9744ee05fffd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316345/field-1/1c985c8ab9f6595267f155c1c2d55523186e5b9f7a2b779f2a5f7673f6c4ac53" :answer-field/choices ["q-316345/field-1/1c985c8ab9f6595267f155c1c2d55523186e5b9f7a2b779f2a5f7673f6c4ac53" "q-316345/field-1/1ecb89157a2da3b6e808df0f3926c29bf711ed3aea432ed0b84fde5c0990b06c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316345" :question/id #uuid "e3c4d97e-d0be-5d30-91d4-65d1d35d63f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-316345" :question/problem "Calculate the area $A$ of the parallelogram spanned by $a=⟨-3,5,0⟩$ and $b=⟨4,-1,2⟩.$\n\n$A=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(5\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-1))i-((-3)\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 4)j+((-3)\\cdot (-1)-5\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =10i+6j-17k \\\\  & =⟨10,6,-17⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{10}^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-17)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100+36+289} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{425} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{17}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-316345/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88dd688-449b-5a6d-8b91-78d00d0c932b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316345"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-19997/selection/f169f92c1946b4a86dcd40a5cae1a30ea50a84a49ecc59038782fea0bf2058cc" :answer/id #uuid "3e89e2d8-dda7-5847-8b77-b5eca3512914" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19997/selection/22808498a9dab5f502b3c6caf3659d3c09bea7d00272f28e595a91887b73521c" :answer/id #uuid "f5bff021-aa1a-5b46-9cfe-2ad2bf41c01e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19997/selection/b336fe0bb5249057b2ff0ec170d4f4011a59ade6c56e9a4ab5b5763d0144b9f6" :answer/id #uuid "d38ca7c6-4181-5520-8349-a4e7559950fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19997/selection/bb5e3e524771fed0f8298cd585cdb5759ed07bb1ac0ac034d00b73a0b668a9ce" :answer/id #uuid "0e10e4d0-2be9-5315-ba11-83e7b39f9839" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19997/selection/a038cf4df09c65d711c1174200281cc22b8be446497e9dc942f4f18d8fa119e2" :answer/id #uuid "4a4b9950-88a2-5498-b7b1-51e2c07dc837" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-19997/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a22d1f8f-236d-5c0b-a357-4561ea1884bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-19997/selection/b336fe0bb5249057b2ff0ec170d4f4011a59ade6c56e9a4ab5b5763d0144b9f6" :answer-field/choices ["q-19997/selection/f169f92c1946b4a86dcd40a5cae1a30ea50a84a49ecc59038782fea0bf2058cc" "q-19997/selection/22808498a9dab5f502b3c6caf3659d3c09bea7d00272f28e595a91887b73521c" "q-19997/selection/b336fe0bb5249057b2ff0ec170d4f4011a59ade6c56e9a4ab5b5763d0144b9f6" "q-19997/selection/bb5e3e524771fed0f8298cd585cdb5759ed07bb1ac0ac034d00b73a0b668a9ce" "q-19997/selection/a038cf4df09c65d711c1174200281cc22b8be446497e9dc942f4f18d8fa119e2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-19997" :question/id #uuid "cf4fff7e-925e-5acf-87a7-2d8a9b262b68" :question/math-academy-id "q-19997" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $f=⟨1,1,-2⟩$ and $g=⟨3,2,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f\\times g & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-2))i-(1\\cdot 1-3\\cdot (-2))j+(1\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 1)k \\\\  & =5i-7j-k \\\\  & =⟨5,-7,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,f\\times g\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-7)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{75} \\\\  & =5\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-19997/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88dd688-449b-5a6d-8b91-78d00d0c932b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-19997"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-19983"] :question/problem "Calculate the area of the triangle spanned by $a=⟨1,3,2⟩$ and $b=⟨4,1,-2⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\times b & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 1 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot (-2)-1\\cdot 2)i-(1\\cdot (-2)-4\\cdot 2)j+(1\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 3)k \\\\  & =-8i+10j-11k \\\\  & =⟨-8,10,-11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,a\\times b\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-8)^{2}+{10}^{2}+(-11)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{285}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of the triangle is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{285}}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-20004/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "cc54fd9d-dcd2-52e2-ab84-110729949a92" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20004/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "e727f4de-80b1-5668-bb51-4412408e53ec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20004/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" :answer/id #uuid "205b61a5-8949-5423-8281-afcba96797f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20004/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" :answer/id #uuid "2515469e-83ab-55f5-a735-b7d5f69a932d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20004/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "828a1e6b-d38f-53ef-a516-82a51a76f1d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-20004/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "abdf458d-1e27-5d4d-8c4c-d16b18dcceb4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-20004/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-20004/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-20004/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-20004/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" "q-20004/selection/04ab8c59d12921ca2d995f79fd8be713086563c65c468afaa0d4bd8ea5bfffaf" "q-20004/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-20004" :question/id #uuid "82a02d55-5cf1-5c0f-a221-1348316193e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-20004" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the parallelogram spanned by $h=⟨2,0,3⟩$ and $l=⟨4,1,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "Using the formula, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h\\times l & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0\\cdot 3-1\\cdot 3)i-(2\\cdot 3-4\\cdot 3)j+(2\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 0)k \\\\  & =-3i+6j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-3,6,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the corresponding parallelogram is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\,h\\times l\\,| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-20004/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f88dd688-449b-5a6d-8b91-78d00d0c932b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-20004"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316516/field-1/a7cf52597248c6a3355c94ca6dd6b886ce545461c345a909a14f79dc3b241fc5" :answer/id #uuid "ff6ddf09-066e-512a-a429-81bfcdd1f732" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{146}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316516/field-1/e777f41c0e8bccdd1c54f16ea0ca8d5a45a8d4390fe17bd33384b645d44fa8c3" :answer/id #uuid "518cff0d-0286-52e8-b06c-5af6bf5f4b2b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{146}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316516/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "03a17ae0-6bb3-5fe4-8600-6619de3d233a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316516/field-1/a7cf52597248c6a3355c94ca6dd6b886ce545461c345a909a14f79dc3b241fc5" :answer-field/choices ["q-316516/field-1/a7cf52597248c6a3355c94ca6dd6b886ce545461c345a909a14f79dc3b241fc5" "q-316516/field-1/e777f41c0e8bccdd1c54f16ea0ca8d5a45a8d4390fe17bd33384b645d44fa8c3"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316516" :question/id #uuid "a30231bb-0a82-5e83-8b1b-9fc734d95002" :question/math-academy-id "q-316516" :question/problem "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the $△\\,LMN$, if $L(1,0,-1)$, $M(3,2,0)$, $N(0,1,3).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =m-l \\\\  & =(3i+2j)-(i-k) \\\\  & =2i+2j+k \\\\  & =⟨2,2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =n-l \\\\  & =(j+3k)-(i-k) \\\\  & =-i+j+4k \\\\  & =⟨-1,1,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 1)i-(2\\cdot 4-(-1)\\cdot 1)j+(2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =7i-9j+4k \\\\  & =⟨7,-9,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{7}^{2}+(-9)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{146}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,LMN$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{146}}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-316516/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316516"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-127908/selection/e4b293d800211720b06f855fe53edb37d197d04a47bf418e078b6d5657f50e60" :answer/id #uuid "2bc6ba1c-d0b6-5cfa-a5ea-1de5c0be7e5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{21}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127908/selection/94ee027a688ca91424939a0f105bbb941a9fc5dced1e94113427147a36e2ec8f" :answer/id #uuid "929d8742-8362-5df3-8fe1-96224a6cc0ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127908/selection/539a2a78543f2770355c2dd0e8aba9dc4c38c69e2526206b8cac8c4c60782484" :answer/id #uuid "2256c129-2c25-52b1-9888-e1dac674e987" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127908/selection/02b74bfbac78e36a02b24ede33c72f7aed7c557e098007f0c167b3ea1fec5070" :answer/id #uuid "456be434-320b-533f-a895-738ed24c51ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{17}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127908/selection/2d7938b36b9b608f1e882bd61e1f0c4189e0dfa0f27d73e4e30bacb9a2a85078" :answer/id #uuid "dd00feb5-9a4c-55cb-b73f-45248954748a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127908/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d72d58ea-9c27-534b-a1db-17d7b5f48986" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127908/selection/2d7938b36b9b608f1e882bd61e1f0c4189e0dfa0f27d73e4e30bacb9a2a85078" :answer-field/choices ["q-127908/selection/e4b293d800211720b06f855fe53edb37d197d04a47bf418e078b6d5657f50e60" "q-127908/selection/94ee027a688ca91424939a0f105bbb941a9fc5dced1e94113427147a36e2ec8f" "q-127908/selection/539a2a78543f2770355c2dd0e8aba9dc4c38c69e2526206b8cac8c4c60782484" "q-127908/selection/02b74bfbac78e36a02b24ede33c72f7aed7c557e098007f0c167b3ea1fec5070" "q-127908/selection/2d7938b36b9b608f1e882bd61e1f0c4189e0dfa0f27d73e4e30bacb9a2a85078"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127908" :question/id #uuid "bfab2245-23fe-5c53-b308-d8d34e386f62" :question/math-academy-id "q-127908" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,PQR,$ if $P(2,6,6),$ $Q(4,8,2),$ $R(0,5,6).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =q-p \\\\  & =(4i+8j+2k)-(2i+6j+6k) \\\\  & =2i+2j-4k \\\\  & =⟨2,2,-4⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =r-p \\\\  & =(5j+6k)-(2i+6j+6k) \\\\  & =-2i-j \\\\  & =⟨-2,-1,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & -1 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot 0-(-1)\\cdot (-4))i-(2\\cdot 0-(-2)\\cdot (-4))j+(2\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-4i+8j+2k \\\\  & =⟨-4,8,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{PR}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\times \\overset{\\to }{PR}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+{8}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{84} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,PQR$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{21}}{2}=\\sqrt{21}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127908/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127908"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71106/selection/3c91eba71fd0d6f8ef73d08542bb8ccc565e26fa8c2f9fd30ca8d458b5591d32" :answer/id #uuid "4d4b3873-3816-51fe-a8b9-66fb999d9db5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{261}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71106/selection/7f76893339431fbe1025dfc34a81e64480edf5168d046d69b36669516297505c" :answer/id #uuid "e4b2dd81-ed03-519d-a622-949fe48b49a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71106/selection/94d169488b0d20e75b8209309c084c190aee315e514e7c4539f5bd12bdad6693" :answer/id #uuid "448590ed-c043-571e-92fd-fddb137e21fe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{97}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71106/selection/db3babdc233009c9211f7b76bc366670e92fb1a2f2a8c5ccfb158ca3e98ca8b2" :answer/id #uuid "64efa9cf-2413-5b8e-8d65-cd7c2c3eb9e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{15}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71106/selection/75976525547cc02ca6c4ff629d65dddba0670b0a9b8e61f2c8bd11d4da98040d" :answer/id #uuid "df6e4e64-2172-5c8d-91ba-a2d7ff4a1dc3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{261}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71106/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4897f82c-d035-54b5-8b75-6c07fe294ed9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71106/selection/75976525547cc02ca6c4ff629d65dddba0670b0a9b8e61f2c8bd11d4da98040d" :answer-field/choices ["q-71106/selection/3c91eba71fd0d6f8ef73d08542bb8ccc565e26fa8c2f9fd30ca8d458b5591d32" "q-71106/selection/7f76893339431fbe1025dfc34a81e64480edf5168d046d69b36669516297505c" "q-71106/selection/94d169488b0d20e75b8209309c084c190aee315e514e7c4539f5bd12bdad6693" "q-71106/selection/db3babdc233009c9211f7b76bc366670e92fb1a2f2a8c5ccfb158ca3e98ca8b2" "q-71106/selection/75976525547cc02ca6c4ff629d65dddba0670b0a9b8e61f2c8bd11d4da98040d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71106" :question/id #uuid "459fa807-906b-5d2b-b3d7-764be7e6e1af" :question/math-academy-id "q-71106" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,WXY$, if $W(2,-3,1)$, $X(-2,1,2)$, $Y(3,-1,3).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{WX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WY}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WX} & =x-w \\\\  & =(-2i+j+2k)-(2i-3j+k) \\\\  & =-4i+4j+k \\\\  & =⟨-4,4,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{WY} & =y-w \\\\  & =(3i-j+3k)-(2i-3j+k) \\\\  & =i+2j+2k \\\\  & =⟨1,2,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{WX}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WY} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -4 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 2)i-((-4)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)j+((-4)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 4)k \\\\  & =6i+9j-12k \\\\  & =⟨6,9,-12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{WX}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{WY}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{WX}\\times \\overset{\\to }{WY}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{9}^{2}+{12}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{261}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,WXY$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{261}}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71106/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71106"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316514/field-1/c7b26da3028a63fbade57242251dcfbe1fd5d9679583a6a464d43138fd704091" :answer/id #uuid "f25e2f6a-436b-5a3f-b0e1-fb372be381c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316514/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "ef1659ce-7e23-5a54-b9ce-83fd92f4fde4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316514/field-1/c7b26da3028a63fbade57242251dcfbe1fd5d9679583a6a464d43138fd704091" :answer-field/choices ["q-316514/field-1/c7b26da3028a63fbade57242251dcfbe1fd5d9679583a6a464d43138fd704091"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316514" :question/id #uuid "40e09c5c-26ee-5c5d-95a4-3eeb7cecfa21" :question/math-academy-id "q-316514" :question/problem "Calculate the area ${A}_{△}$ of the $△\\,DEF$, if $D(-1,2,0)$, $E(2,0,1)$, $F(1,3,2).$\n\n${A}_{△}=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE} & =e-d \\\\  & =(2i+k)-(-i+2j) \\\\  & =3i-2j+k \\\\  & =⟨3,-2,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =f-d \\\\  & =(i+3j+2k)-(-i+2j) \\\\  & =2i+j+2k \\\\  & =⟨2,1,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\times \\overset{\\to }{DF} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 1)i-(3\\cdot 2-2\\cdot 1)j+(3\\cdot 1-(-2)\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =-5i-4j+7k \\\\  & =⟨-5,-4,7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{DE}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{DF}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{DE}\\times \\overset{\\to }{DF}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+{7}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{90} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,DEF$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{3\\sqrt{10}}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-316514/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316514"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71109/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" :answer/id #uuid "93b51b29-107a-5e83-9361-0ae10849dcec" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71109/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" :answer/id #uuid "ad2cb831-b288-5802-ae8b-b70af46cfa46" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71109/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "328d90d9-b0a9-5d4b-933a-c42ad2baaaf3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71109/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "88eda209-592f-5f8a-8830-7f9154b7d541" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71109/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer/id #uuid "7e49239d-e14f-50c7-8be0-07559990fc0e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71109/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b71a137-9d32-5a04-9e94-18b613936f62" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71109/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9" :answer-field/choices ["q-71109/selection/e7f6c27482797e11bd6b0013338edc6789517ab47eb94f4fe9912fc5f8b6c4b8" "q-71109/selection/2edf353dc47d221855e5e7ee4be942392390ff01766e089c29dc368c2051b12d" "q-71109/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-71109/selection/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" "q-71109/selection/e014eef6d5b5b99f76a63badf4d7e4589d1524a951e6f15c41809dcf478e3da9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71109" :question/id #uuid "2323e41e-94b0-58fe-ac87-5b4350006c14" :question/math-academy-id "q-71109" :question/problem "Calculate the area of the $△\\,FGH$, if $F(1,1,2)$, $G(2,2,3)$, $H(1,0,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{FG}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{FH}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FG} & =g-f \\\\  & =(2i+2j+3k)-(i+j+2k) \\\\  & =i+j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{FH} & =h-f \\\\  & =(i+k)-(i+j+2k) \\\\  & =-j-k \\\\  & =⟨0,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula to compute the cross product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{FG}\\times \\overset{\\to }{FH} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(1\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 1)i-(1\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot 1)j+(1\\cdot (-1)-0\\cdot 1)k \\\\  & =j-k \\\\  & =⟨0,1,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{FG}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{FH}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{FG}\\times \\overset{\\to }{FH}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,FGH$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-71109/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7c30217a-484c-5c31-a2bf-413f04e0edea"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71109"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316400/field-1/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" :answer/id #uuid "191fcae2-d836-58ef-9d69-61b65efd3a47" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316400/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa" :answer/id #uuid "93aa79ec-e915-5f14-9f4c-312bdc534daf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316400/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "28caeb49-f626-584b-aecf-3deecd660070" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316400/field-1/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" :answer-field/choices ["q-316400/field-1/9f6bfd6fa85d96298a99db901d9b73f609ef64ac0bcf5fbdc4a7ac6d3b733558" "q-316400/field-1/a0e0e68f25b8b46aafef3b74aff7beff7fddc6de5bf36921680b04c7b0e6ffaa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316400" :question/id #uuid "739d9a68-e221-5a5d-8937-f863ef4887e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-316400" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $VL$ of the $△\\,TUV$, if $T(1,0,1)$, $U(3,2,-1)$, $V(-1,1,0).$\n\n$VL=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $VL$ can be related to the area of $△\\,TUV$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}VL\\cdot TU\n$$\n\nSo, to find $VL,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{TU}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{TV}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TU} & =u-t \\\\  & =(3i+2j-k)-(i+k) \\\\  & =2i+2j-2k \\\\  & =⟨2,2,-2⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{TV} & =v-t \\\\  & =(-i+j)-(i+k) \\\\  & =-2i+j-k \\\\  & =⟨-2,1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TU}\\times \\overset{\\to }{TV} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(2\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot 1)i-(2\\cdot (-1)-(-2)\\cdot (-2))j+(2\\cdot 1-2\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =0i+6j+6k \\\\  & =⟨0,6,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{TU}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{TV}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{TU}\\times \\overset{\\to }{TV}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{6}^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{72} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,TUV$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{6\\sqrt{2}}{2}=3\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $TU$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TU & =|\\overset{\\to }{TU}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{12} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}VL\\cdot TU,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}VL\\cdot TU \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}VL\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{2} & =VL\\cdot \\sqrt{3} \\\\ VL & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ VL & =\\sqrt{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-316400/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9331987e-8676-5bdb-b4ce-2129b1b09a8c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316400"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316558/field-1/d1f4947b6216525120d57205e16b828a1d6b415d3fb273ca3e61f89106a3c324" :answer/id #uuid "96671eca-6ca7-54fa-b17a-3158e5027494" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9\\sqrt{22}}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316558/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "62ecc290-691b-5d71-a44a-6409725d632a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316558/field-1/d1f4947b6216525120d57205e16b828a1d6b415d3fb273ca3e61f89106a3c324" :answer-field/choices ["q-316558/field-1/d1f4947b6216525120d57205e16b828a1d6b415d3fb273ca3e61f89106a3c324"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316558" :question/id #uuid "12a34565-5a9f-56ec-9dc5-8c09530cec82" :question/math-academy-id "q-316558" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $TK$ of the $△\\,RST,$ if $R(4,5,6),$ $S(7,4,5),$ $T(6,8,4).$\n\n$TK=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $TK$ can be related to the area of $△\\,RST$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}TK\\cdot RS\n$$\n\nSo, to find $TK,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{RS}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RT}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RS} & =s-r \\\\  & =(7i+4j+5k)-(4i+5j+6k) \\\\  & =3i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨3,-1,-1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{RT} & =t-r \\\\  & =(6i+8j+4k)-(4i+5j+6k) \\\\  & =2i+3j-2k \\\\  & =⟨2,3,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{RS}\\times \\overset{\\to }{RT} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & -2\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)(-2)-(-1)\\cdot 3)i-(3(-2)-(-1)\\cdot 2)j+(3\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot 2)k \\\\  & =5i+4j+11k \\\\  & =⟨5,4,11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{RS}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{RT}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{RS}\\times \\overset{\\to }{RT}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{11}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{162} \\\\  & =9\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,RST$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $RS$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RS & =|\\overset{\\to }{RS}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}TK\\cdot RS,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}TK\\cdot \\sqrt{11} \\\\ TK & =\\frac{9\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{11}} \\\\ TK & =\\frac{9\\sqrt{22}}{11}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-316558/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9331987e-8676-5bdb-b4ce-2129b1b09a8c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-316558"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-316392/field-1/b17f3adae995204daa21239edeef0c002350bf80ec7d546eae745741dde2333c" :answer/id #uuid "cf94084a-72d7-52a5-8771-e8eafe06c86c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3230}}{19}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316392/field-1/0caf5f256c458cf37e26bc6688f1714d1f75a331d86c1d2dfdbf951742640bc0" :answer/id #uuid "c57cba44-a61e-5597-ad1e-b5d128532128" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{170}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-316392/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "571366c2-95fe-5e22-a02e-0748b17c58ba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-316392/field-1/b17f3adae995204daa21239edeef0c002350bf80ec7d546eae745741dde2333c" :answer-field/choices ["q-316392/field-1/b17f3adae995204daa21239edeef0c002350bf80ec7d546eae745741dde2333c" "q-316392/field-1/0caf5f256c458cf37e26bc6688f1714d1f75a331d86c1d2dfdbf951742640bc0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-316392" :question/id #uuid "a455fd9d-8822-5b05-916e-ddb6e1245874" :question/math-academy-id "q-316392" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $NP$ of the $△\\,LMN$, if $L(3,-1,0)$, $M(0,2,1)$, $N(-2,1,-1).$\n\n$NP=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $NP$ can be related to the area of $△\\,LMN$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,NP\\cdot LM.\n$$\n\nSo, to find $NP,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM} & =m-l \\\\  & =(2j+k)-(3i-j) \\\\  & =-3i+3j+k \\\\  & =⟨-3,3,1⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =n-l \\\\  & =(-2i+j-k)-(3i-j) \\\\  & =-5i+2j-k \\\\  & =⟨-5,2,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 1 \\\\ -5 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot 2)i-((-3)\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot (-5))j+((-3)\\cdot 2-3\\cdot (-5))k \\\\  & =-5i-8j+9k \\\\  & =⟨-5,-8,9⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{LM}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{LN}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{LM}\\times \\overset{\\to }{LN}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(-8)^{2}+{9}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{170}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,LMN$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{\\sqrt{170}}{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $LM$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}LM & =|\\overset{\\to }{LM}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}\\,NP\\cdot LM,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,NP\\cdot LM \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{170}}{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\,NP\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ \\sqrt{170} & =NP\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ NP & =\\frac{\\sqrt{170}}{\\sqrt{19}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3230}}{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-316392/field-1"] 