" "q-128006/selection/df4166f6d3a2e3c4b3bd502dbf4758b242421161f75fcec236ae68e36e33cd34" "q-128006/selection/0f2efb815c865f4e16b2c4411ac634759ffba1246c55888ad6706d91bc07b570"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-128006" :question/id #uuid "baa1ec57-d442-586e-ad16-7b7f53918a50" :question/math-academy-id "q-128006" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $CH$ of the $△\\,ABC,$ if $A(4,-1,1),$ $B(0,-3,4),$ $C(2,1,4).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $CH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,ABC$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB\n$$\n\nSo, to find $CH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =b-a \\\\  & =(-3j+4k)-(4i-j+k) \\\\  & =-4i-2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-4,-2,3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =c-a \\\\  & =(2i+j+4k)-(4i-j+k) \\\\  & =-2i+2j+3k \\\\  & =⟨-2,2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-2)\\cdot 3-2\\cdot 3)i-((-4)\\cdot 3-(-2)\\cdot 3)j+((-4)\\cdot 2-(-2)\\cdot (-2))k \\\\  & =-12i+6j-12k \\\\  & =⟨-12,6,-12⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{AC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}\\times \\overset{\\to }{AC}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-12)^{2}+{6}^{2}+(-12)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{324} \\\\  & =18.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,ABC$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{18}{2}=9.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $AB$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =|\\overset{\\to }{AB}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{29}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot AB \\\\ 9 & =\\frac{1}{2}CH\\cdot \\sqrt{29} \\\\ 18 & =CH\\cdot \\sqrt{29} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{18}{\\sqrt{29}} \\\\ CH & =\\frac{18\\sqrt{29}}{29}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-128006/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9331987e-8676-5bdb-b4ce-2129b1b09a8c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-128006"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-71115/selection/06da2f49274e3e07a60c6b53a4a73849755533085e98fc1f408113be7e9ec35e" :answer/id #uuid "598a4cbe-1616-5202-8c4b-2e91a1be74ab" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{38}}{19}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71115/selection/8e70564eb979b953c8d3990048f4460d115bd79da075968787bcc585d7fc4c43" :answer/id #uuid "66bceb07-b907-51e5-85fd-5a41af17c4d3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{38}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71115/selection/d5440caeb96b92f9a78fbff8e6566e73e6e0c3a29818bb5b7ba83d55fe91488b" :answer/id #uuid "6f7c7a07-9a46-5964-94e5-a57b6d5a41f9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{19}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71115/selection/c8357010f819dc7a7e61ed62bc634b4440880d302930cd997a0e9218660ca0ca" :answer/id #uuid "6a3dbe78-512d-525e-a6f2-3f91df5a5abe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{19}}{19}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71115/selection/8551f4ab982fcde1f823c1977548aa17e8676df39a3695767fd216f31d51658b" :answer/id #uuid "3799f69b-956b-5ca2-89c3-c6f0e082b710" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-71115/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9ec0890c-98ea-5e24-849a-fba7d47e24e4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-71115/selection/06da2f49274e3e07a60c6b53a4a73849755533085e98fc1f408113be7e9ec35e" :answer-field/choices ["q-71115/selection/06da2f49274e3e07a60c6b53a4a73849755533085e98fc1f408113be7e9ec35e" "q-71115/selection/8e70564eb979b953c8d3990048f4460d115bd79da075968787bcc585d7fc4c43" "q-71115/selection/d5440caeb96b92f9a78fbff8e6566e73e6e0c3a29818bb5b7ba83d55fe91488b" "q-71115/selection/c8357010f819dc7a7e61ed62bc634b4440880d302930cd997a0e9218660ca0ca" "q-71115/selection/8551f4ab982fcde1f823c1977548aa17e8676df39a3695767fd216f31d51658b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-71115" :question/id #uuid "1eff474b-577f-5cdd-aedd-f925f884ac47" :question/math-academy-id "q-71115" :question/problem "Calculate the length of the altitude $VH$ of the $△\\,TUV$, if $T(3,2,3)$, $U(0,1,0)$, $V(2,1,2).$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the length of the altitude $VH$ can be related to the area of $△\\,TUV$ as follows:\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}VH\\cdot TU\n$$\n\nSo, to find $VH,$ we first find ${A}_{△}.$ To start, we find the vectors $\\overset{\\to }{TU}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{TV}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TU} & =u-t \\\\  & =j-(3i+2j+3k) \\\\  & =-3i-j-3k \\\\  & =⟨-3,-1,-3⟩ \\\\ \\overset{\\to }{TV} & =v-t \\\\  & =(2i+j+2k)-(3i+2j+3k) \\\\  & =-i-j-k \\\\  & =⟨-1,-1,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{TU}\\times \\overset{\\to }{TV} & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3 & -1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =((-1)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot (-3))i-((-3)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot (-3))j+((-3)\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot (-1))k \\\\  & =-2i+2k \\\\  & =⟨-2,0,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram spanned by $\\overset{\\to }{TU}$ and $\\overset{\\to }{TV}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =|\\overset{\\to }{TU}\\times \\overset{\\to }{TV}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe area of the triangle is half of the area of the respective parallelogram. So, the area of $△\\,TUV$ is\n\n$$\n{A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}A=\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{2}=\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's also compute $TU$ since it appears in the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TU & =|\\overset{\\to }{TU}| \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nFinally, using the formula ${A}_{△}=\\frac{1}{2}VH\\cdot TU,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{△} & =\\frac{1}{2}VH\\cdot TU \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}VH\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & =VH\\cdot \\sqrt{19} \\\\ VH & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{19}} \\\\ VH & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{38}}{19}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-71115/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9331987e-8676-5bdb-b4ce-2129b1b09a8c"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-71115"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
